{"seconds": 1.052773040952161, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/K06/gpt-5-2025-08-07.json", "submission_sha256": "ab79d9a0ddb9d95d54e7af6d7f36870789660cc666d948f3d1f7f3dc7b620da2", "code_sha256": "d04258398b5173b54dd7fe20734d30a9c487f9501a6ca1e7c7d42d25149faf9f", "description": "Mouse-disjoint PV/SST classifier with fixed inner CV model selection. The procedure: (1) build candidates: RBF SVM with C in {0.1,1,10,100} using median imputation + standardization, and ExtraTrees (500 trees, max_features in {sqrt,1}) using median imputation only; all with deterministic seed 20261031 and one numerical CPU thread where applicable. (2) Use the provided three-fold cv_fold to run mouse-disjoint validation. Each fold fits preprocessing on its training partition only. (3) Optimize by the primary class_balanced_mouse_accuracy: accuracy is computed per mouse, averaged across mice within PV and SST separately, then averaged across the two classes. (4) During each fit, derive sample weights from training data only so that every mouse contributes equally within its class and each class sums to equal total weight: for each class, each mouse gets total weight 1/num_mice_in_class, uniformly distributed over its cells. (5) Refit the chosen model on all training data with the same preprocessing and weighting, then predict test labels. Output is a finite integer numpy array of shape (71,) with labels 0=PV, 1=SST. Only training data determine all transforms; group_ids and cv_fold are used solely for CV and weight construction; no test identifiers are used; single-threaded trees; deterministic outcomes.", "code_lines": 170, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

